<span id="S3.F1.pic1.7.2" class="ltx_p">RISC-V Assembly + HEX Files</span>
<span id="S3.F1.pic1.7.3" class="ltx_p">IMEM.hex, DMEM.hex, WMEM.hex, output.S</span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 -16.97 L 0 -80.3"></path><g style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" color="#000000" transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 1.0 0.0 0 -80.3)"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 3.6 0 L -2.16 2.88 L 0 0 L -2.16 -2.88"></path></g></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 -124.53 L 0 -187.86"></path><g style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" color="#000000" transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 1.0 0.0 0 -187.86)"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 3.6 0 L -2.16 2.88 L 0 0 L -2.16 -2.88"></path></g></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 -239.1 L 0 -302.44"></path><g style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" color="#000000" transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 1.0 0.0 0 -302.44)"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 3.6 0 L -2.16 2.88 L 0 0 L -2.16 -2.88"></path></g></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 -353.03 L 0 -416.36"></path><g style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" color="#000000" transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 1.0 0.0 0 -416.36)"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 3.6 0 L -2.16 2.88 L 0 0 L -2.16 -2.88"></path></g></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 -466.95 L 0 -530.29"></path><g style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" color="#000000" transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 1.0 0.0 0 -530.29)"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 3.6 0 L -2.16 2.88 L 0 0 L -2.16 -2.88"></path></g></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 -580.88 L 0 -644.21"></path><g style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" color="#000000" transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 1.0 0.0 0 -644.21)"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 3.6 0 L -2.16 2.88 L 0 0 L -2.16 -2.88"></path></g></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 1: </span>Complete compilation pipeline from ONNX model to ASIC-ready RISC-V assembly</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2 </span>Learned Optimization Framework</h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Traditional auto-tuning relies on analytical cost models that approximate hardware behavior. We introduce a learned cost model that adapts to actual hardware through iterative training.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">3.2.1 </span>Learned Cost Model</h4>

<div id="S3.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The learned cost model uses linear regression with feature extraction:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{T}_{\text{exec}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>exec</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{T}_{\text{exec}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=0}^{n}w_{i}\cdot f_{i}(\text{node},\text{config})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>node</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext>config</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=0}^{n}w_{i}\cdot f_{i}(\text{node},\text{config})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS2.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are features extracted from:</p>
<ul id="S3.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S3.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Configuration parameters (tile sizes, unroll factors, vector length)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Operation characteristics (FLOPs, memory traffic, data types)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Tensor dimensions (shape, size, dimensionality)</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The model trains using gradient descent on collected performance samples:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle w_{i}^{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle w_{i}^{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=w_{i}^{t}-\alpha\cdot\frac{\partial L}{\partial w_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=w_{i}^{t}-\alpha\cdot\frac{\partial L}{\partial w_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS2.SSS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> is the mean squared error between predicted and actual execution times.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">3.2.2 </span>Training Sample Collection</h4>

<div id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">During auto-tuning, each configuration trial generates a training sample:</p>
<ul id="S3.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S3.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Configuration parameters (tile sizes, unroll factors, etc.)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Actual performance metrics (execution time, cycles, memory bandwidth)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Operation signature (operator type, tensor dimensions)</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Samples are collected incrementally and used to refine the model, improving prediction accuracy over time.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">3.2.3 </span>Hybrid Cost Model</h4>

<div id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The compiler supports three cost model modes:</p>
<ol id="S3.I4" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S3.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Analytical</span>: Fast predictions using hardware models, suitable for initial exploration</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S3.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Learned</span>: ML-based predictions after training, higher accuracy for explored configurations</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S3.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I4.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hybrid</span>: Combines analytical and learned models, using learned model for similar configurations and falling back to analytical for novel ones</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2.SSS4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">3.2.4 </span>Multi-Algorithm Auto-Tuning Framework</h4>

<div id="S3.SS2.SSS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Unlike traditional compilers that use a single search strategy, XgenSilicon implements five distinct search algorithms, each optimized for different optimization scenarios:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.SSS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Bayesian Optimization:</span> Uses Gaussian Process (GP) surrogate models with Expected Improvement (EI) acquisition function. The acquisition function balances exploration and exploitation:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{EI}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>EI</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{EI}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(f_{\text{best}}-\mu(x))\cdot\Phi(Z)+\sigma(x)\cdot\phi(Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>best</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(f_{\text{best}}-\mu(x))\cdot\Phi(Z)+\sigma(x)\cdot\phi(Z)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS2.SSS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z=(f_{\text{best}}-\mu(x))/\sigma(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>best</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=(f_{\text{best}}-\mu(x))/\sigma(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS2.SSS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> is the standard normal CDF, and <math id="S3.SS2.SSS4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> is the standard normal PDF. The uncertainty <math id="S3.SS2.SSS4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is estimated using RBF kernel-like behavior based on distance to observed configurations, combined with empirical variance from observed metrics. This approach converges 50-60% faster than analytical models by learning from observed configurations.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.SSS4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Genetic Algorithm:</span> Employs tournament selection, crossover, and mutation with configurable parameters (population size, mutation rate, elite fraction). The algorithm maintains diversity through population-based search, making it effective for multi-modal optimization landscapes. Configuration mutation uses ParameterSpace-aware bounds checking for proper choice selection.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.SSS4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Simulated Annealing:</span> Uses temperature-based acceptance probability for escaping local minima:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS4.p7" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P(\text{accept})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>accept</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P(\text{accept})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\begin{cases}1&amp;\text{if }\Delta E&lt;0\\
\exp(-\Delta E/T)&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>E</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>otherwise</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\begin{cases}1&amp;\text{if }\Delta E&lt;0\\
\exp(-\Delta E/T)&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS4.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS4.p8.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS2.SSS4.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta E</annotation></semantics></math> is the cost difference and <math id="S3.SS2.SSS4.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> is the temperature, which decreases according to a cooling schedule.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS4.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS4.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.SSS4.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Random Search:</span> Provides baseline performance and warm-up samples for Bayesian optimization.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS4.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS4.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.SSS4.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Grid Search:</span> Exhaustive search for small parameter spaces, ensuring global optimum discovery.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS4.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS4.p11.1" class="ltx_p">The compiler automatically selects the appropriate algorithm based on parameter space size, available time budget, and optimization history.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.3 </span>Quantization Framework</h3>

<section id="S3.SS3.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">3.3.1 </span>Post-Training Quantization (PTQ)</h4>

<div id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">PTQ quantizes models using calibration data without retraining. We implement three calibration methods:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">KL Divergence Calibration:</span> Implements a full histogram-based KL divergence minimization algorithm with 2048-bin resolution for high accuracy. The algorithm searches over 100 threshold candidates to find the optimal clipping range:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\text{KL}(P||Q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>KL</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{KL}(P||Q)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i}P(i)\log\frac{P(i)}{Q(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i}P(i)\log\frac{P(i)}{Q(i)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> is the original FP32 activation distribution and <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> is the quantized distribution. The algorithm builds reference histograms, simulates quantization for each threshold, computes KL divergence, and selects the threshold minimizing information loss. This full implementation provides superior accuracy compared to simplified percentile-based methods.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Percentile Calibration:</span> Uses configurable percentile (default 99.9th) as clipping threshold, robust to outliers:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="S3.E6.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">clip_max</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{percentile}(\text{activations},p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>percentile</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>activations</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{percentile}(\text{activations},p)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Entropy Calibration:</span> Maximizes information preservation by optimizing for entropy:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle H(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle H(X)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E7.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\sum_{i}P(x_{i})\log P(x_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\sum_{i}P(x_{i})\log P(x_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">3.3.2 </span>Quantization-Aware Training (QAT)</h4>

<div id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">QAT inserts fake quantization nodes (quantize-dequantize pairs) that preserve gradients during training:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{FakeQuant}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>FakeQuant</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{FakeQuant}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{Dequantize}(\text{Quantize}(x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Dequantize</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>Quantize</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{Dequantize}(\text{Quantize}(x))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The straight-through estimator allows gradients to flow through quantization:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial L}{\partial x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial L}{\partial x}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\partial L}{\partial\text{FakeQuant}(x)}\cdot\frac{\partial\text{FakeQuant}(x)}{\partial x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mtext>FakeQuant</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mtext>FakeQuant</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\partial L}{\partial\text{FakeQuant}(x)}\cdot\frac{\partial\text{FakeQuant}(x)}{\partial x}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\text{FakeQuant}(x)}{\partial x}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mtext>FakeQuant</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\text{FakeQuant}(x)}{\partial x}=1</annotation></semantics></math> (straight-through).</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Quantization parameters (scale, zero_point) are updated using full gradient computation with momentum:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial L}{\partial\text{scale}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mtext>scale</mtext></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial L}{\partial\text{scale}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i}\frac{\partial L}{\partial x_{\text{deq}}}\cdot(q_{i}-\text{zp})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mtext>deq</mtext></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mtext>zp</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i}\frac{\partial L}{\partial x_{\text{deq}}}\cdot(q_{i}-\text{zp})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial L}{\partial\text{zp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mtext>zp</mtext></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial L}{\partial\text{zp}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i}\frac{\partial L}{\partial x_{\text{deq}}}\cdot(-\text{scale})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mtext>deq</mtext></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mtext>scale</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i}\frac{\partial L}{\partial x_{\text{deq}}}\cdot(-\text{scale})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v_{\text{scale}}^{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mtext>scale</mtext><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v_{\text{scale}}^{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\beta\cdot v_{\text{scale}}^{t}+(1-\beta)\cdot\frac{\partial L}{\partial\text{scale}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mtext>scale</mtext><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mtext>scale</mtext></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\beta\cdot v_{\text{scale}}^{t}+(1-\beta)\cdot\frac{\partial L}{\partial\text{scale}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{scale}^{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mtext>scale</mtext><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{scale}^{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{scale}^{t}-\alpha\cdot v_{\text{scale}}^{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mtext>scale</mtext><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mtext>scale</mtext><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{scale}^{t}-\alpha\cdot v_{\text{scale}}^{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the quantized value, <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> is the momentum term with coefficient <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=0.9</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> is the learning rate. This full implementation with momentum provides stable convergence compared to simple gradient descent.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">3.3.3 </span>Supported Precisions</h4>

<div id="S3.SS3.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S3.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 3.3.3 Supported Precisions ‣ 3.3 Quantization Framework ‣ 3 Compiler Architecture ‣ Hardware-Aware Neural Network Compilation with Learned Optimization:A RISC-V Accelerator Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> shows all supported precisions and their characteristics.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.T2" class="ltx_table">
<table id="S3.T2.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S3.T2.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S3.T2.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_t"><span id="S3.T2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Precision</span></th>
<th id="S3.T2.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t"><span id="S3.T2.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Bits</span></th>
<th id="S3.T2.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t"><span id="S3.T2.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Bytes</span></th>
<th id="S3.T2.2.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t"><span id="S3.T2.2.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Compression</span></th>
<th id="S3.T2.2.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t"><span id="S3.T2.2.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Use Case</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S3.T2.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S3.T2.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">FP32</th>
<td id="S3.T2.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">32</td>
