</tbody>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span>Supported precisions and compression ratios</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.SSS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Brain Float 16 (BF16) Support:</span> XgenSilicon implements full BF16 support with dedicated quantization and dequantization functions. BF16 uses the same 8-bit exponent as FP32 but with a 7-bit mantissa (same as FP16), providing better training stability than FP16 while maintaining the same memory footprint. The compiler implements efficient FP32-to-BF16 conversion by truncating the lower 16 bits of the FP32 representation, and BF16-to-FP32 conversion by zero-padding the lower mantissa bits. This precision is particularly valuable for training workloads where numerical stability is critical, as BF16 preserves the dynamic range of FP32 while reducing memory requirements by 2×.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.4 </span>RISC-V Vector Optimizations</h3>

<section id="S3.SS4.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">3.4.1 </span>Register Grouping (LMUL)</h4>

<div id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The RISC-V Vector extension supports LMUL (register grouping) to process more elements per instruction:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="S3.E14.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">elements_processed</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{VL}\times\text{LMUL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>VL</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext>LMUL</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{VL}\times\text{LMUL}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The compiler automatically selects optimal LMUL based on:</p>
<ul id="S3.I5" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S3.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Data type size (smaller types benefit from higher LMUL)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Operation characteristics (elementwise operations use higher LMUL)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I5.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I5.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I5.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Register availability</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS4.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">3.4.2 </span>Loop Unrolling</h4>

<div id="S3.SS4.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Unrolling reduces loop overhead and improves instruction-level parallelism. The compiler determines unroll factors based on:</p>
<ul id="S3.I6" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S3.I6.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I6.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I6.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Loop trip count (smaller loops benefit from full unrolling)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I6.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I6.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I6.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Register pressure (balance unrolling with register availability)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I6.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I6.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I6.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Cache behavior (unrolling improves temporal locality)</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS4.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">3.4.3 </span>Register Tiling</h4>

<div id="S3.SS4.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Matrix operations are tiled to fit in registers, improving cache locality:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="S3.E15.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">Tile Size</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\arg\min_{t}\text{Memory Traffic}(t)+\lambda\cdot\text{Register Pressure}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mi>t</mi></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>Memory Traffic</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>Register Pressure</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\arg\min_{t}\text{Memory Traffic}(t)+\lambda\cdot\text{Register Pressure}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.SSS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.SSS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The compiler uses auto-tuning to find optimal tile sizes for each operation type.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.5 </span>Dynamic Shape Support</h3>

<div id="S3.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">XgenSilicon supports dynamic shapes through symbolic dimensions and runtime shape resolution. The compiler:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="S3.I7" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S3.I7.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I7.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I7.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I7.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Symbolic Dimensions</span>: Allows dimensions to be specified as ranges (e.g., batch size 1-32, sequence length 128-512)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I7.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I7.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I7.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I7.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Graph Cloning</span>: Clones the computation graph with symbolic dimensions marked as -1, preserving all nodes, tensors, and initializers</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I7.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I7.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I7.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I7.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Runtime Resolution</span>: Generates RISC-V assembly code for runtime shape dimension resolution</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I7.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I7.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I7.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I7.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Shape Specialization</span>: Creates multiple specialized versions for common shape configurations, selecting the appropriate version at runtime</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I7.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I7.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I7.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I7.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Shape Validation</span>: Generates runtime shape checking code to validate input shapes before execution</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The compiler handles dynamic shapes by marking symbolic dimensions as -1 in tensor shapes, then generating specialized code paths for runtime shape resolution. This enables efficient handling of variable batch sizes, sequence lengths, and other dynamic dimensions common in ML workloads.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.6 </span>Hardware Validation</h3>

<div id="S3.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Unlike general-purpose compilers, XgenSilicon includes built-in hardware validation:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">ISA Validation:</span> Ensures all generated instructions comply with the target hardware’s 61-instruction ISA, checking:</p>
<ul id="S3.I8" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S3.I8.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I8.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I8.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Instruction encoding correctness</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I8.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I8.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I8.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Register usage (no register spills beyond available registers)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I8.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I8.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I8.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Immediate value ranges</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I8.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I8.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I8.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Instruction legality (no unsupported instruction combinations)</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS6.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS6.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Memory Validation:</span> Checks memory constraints:</p>
<ul id="S3.I9" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S3.I9.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I9.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I9.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">DMEM size limits (activation buffer constraints)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I9.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I9.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I9.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">WMEM size limits (weight storage constraints)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I9.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I9.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I9.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Address alignment requirements</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I9.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I9.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I9.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Memory access patterns (no out-of-bounds accesses)</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS6.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Validation failures are reported with detailed error messages, preventing runtime errors on hardware.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.7 </span>Advanced Cache-Aware Cost Modeling</h3>

<div id="S3.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The compiler implements full cache hit rate estimation that considers multiple factors:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS7.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS7.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS7.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Access Pattern Analysis:</span> Distinguishes between sequential (MatMul, Conv, elementwise) and random access patterns, adjusting hit rates accordingly. Sequential operations achieve 95% L1 hit rate, while random access patterns achieve 70% L1 hit rate.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS7.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS7.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS7.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Tiling Effectiveness:</span> Computes tile effectiveness based on tile sizes relative to cache sizes. Tiling can improve hit rates by up to 15% by keeping working sets in cache.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS7.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS7.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS7.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Multi-Level Cache Hierarchy:</span> Computes weighted average hit rates across L1, L2, and L3 caches based on working set size:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS7.p5" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="S3.E16.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">Hit Rate</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{3}\text{portion}_{i}\cdot\text{hit\_rate}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></munderover></mstyle><msub><mtext>portion</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mtext>hit_rate</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{3}\text{portion}_{i}\cdot\text{hit\_rate}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS7.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS7.p6.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS7.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{portion}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>portion</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{portion}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the fraction of data in cache level <math id="S3.SS7.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. This provides accurate performance predictions for memory-bound operations.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Experimental Evaluation</h2>

<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1 </span>Experimental Setup</h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate XgenSilicon ML Compiler on:</p>
<ul id="S4.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Models</span>: ResNet-50, MobileNet-V2, BERT-base, Vision Transformer</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hardware Target</span>: Custom RISC-V RV32I + RVV accelerator</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Baselines</span>: Standard off-the-shelf CPU (ARM Cortex-A78), hand-designed ASIC</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Metrics</span>: Execution time, power consumption, silicon area</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
